use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../../behaviors/FormParticipation import FormParticipation
from ../../buttons/Button import Button

export ui-component FilePicker:
    description:
        A file picker is a button that opens the device's own file chooser and
        hands back the files the user picked. It can limit which kinds of file
        are offered, and allow one file or several.

    composes:
        - @{Button}

    behaviors:
        - @{FormParticipation}

    picking:
        Pressing the button opens the device's file chooser. If the user
        cancels, nothing changes. By default, picking again replaces the
        earlier choice. The component can instead add to it, up to its limit,
        and let the user remove files one at a time.

    fileTypes:
        The component can say which kinds of file to offer, such as images
        only. This is a hint to the file chooser, and on some platforms the
        user can get around it, so the files handed back are still checked.

    limits:
        Besides the kinds of file, the component can limit how many files can
        be picked, and how large or small each one can be, and can add its own
        checks. The component is told which files were accepted, and which
        were turned away and why, such as being too large or too many.

    camera:
        On devices with a camera, the component can ask for the camera to be
        offered straight away, such as for a photo of a receipt. Whether this
        works is up to the chosen library and platform.

    chosen:
        After picking, it shows what was chosen, such as the file name or "3
        files", and lets the user clear the choice. A disabled or read-only
        file picker keeps showing what was chosen, but it can't be changed.

    nonGoals:
        - No uploading, progress bars, or previews. It only hands back the files
        - Whether folders can be picked is up to the chosen library and
            platform
